Hello Gabriel,

Occupancy models will not give you abundance, only the proportion of your sites where the species is present.  To get abundance (density is abundance/area), you'll need to use N-mix models.  I found the vignettes included with the R package very helpful when I was starting out.  There are also lots of free online resources for the basics of R.

-Alex

